// Title: Potentially Suspicious Child Processes Spawned by ConHost
// ID: dfa03a09-8b92-4d83-8e74-f72839b1c407
// Status: experimental
// Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2025-02-05
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1202, attack.t1218
// Description: Detects suspicious child processes related to Windows Shell utilities spawned by `conhost.exe`, which could indicate malicious activity using trusted system components.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\cmd.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\cscript.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\mshta.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\powershell_ise.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\powershell.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\pwsh.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\regsvr32.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\wscript.exe")) OR ((OriginalFileName = "cmd.exe" OR OriginalFileName = "cscript.exe" OR OriginalFileName = "mshta.exe" OR OriginalFileName = "powershell_ise.exe" OR OriginalFileName = "powershell.exe" OR OriginalFileName = "pwsh.dll" OR OriginalFileName = "regsvr32.exe" OR OriginalFileName = "wscript.exe"))) AND (src.process.parent.image.path endswithCIS "\\conhost.exe"))
